From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:07:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [SDL3-DOS] dos: patch 0143 --
 SDL_DOSAudioSetContentActive: the SB silence gate keeps a sound's own silence

WHY DOS NEEDS THIS: DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice's post-mix silence gate
(SDL/0054, "Shape A") drops every buffer that is silent in the DEVICE
format instead of writing it to the ring. Between sounds that is its
purpose (the ring drains; with idle-pause enabled the DSP pauses).
During a sound it removes time, in two forms:
  (a) a clip's own digital-zero stretches are dropped on every path;
  (b) on the 8-bit path, SDL's F32 -> U8 conversion rounds |s| < 128 (of
      32768) to 0x80, so every chunk quieter than ~-48 dBFS is also
      "silent" and dropped.
A dropped chunk either becomes a silent IRQ (ring empty: timing kept,
but counted as a dropout by any port that watches silent IRQs) or, with
audio queued behind it, the next audible chunk plays early and the
clip's pauses shrink.

Evidence (dosags, PLAN.md step 8, "Sound-9 / dropout investigation",
2026-09-22):
  - Real hardware (8.3 round, PicoGUS in SB mode on the 8-bit path; the
    defect, not the fix): ~50 silent IRQs per play of 5 Days a Stranger's
    sound 9, whose 4.10 s clip is 52 of 88 512-sample windows exact
    digital zero -- the "dropouts" were the clip's own silence; expected
    vs played PCM chunks 1617 vs 1513 and 1304 vs 1199 in two runs; sound
    10 (9.76 s) played ~9.0 s against ~10.0 s in the DOSBox-X reference.
  - DOSBox-X --sb-live, throwaway chunk classifier (UR8): chunk accounting
    is exact -- 16-bit path pcm IRQs 582 = 639 mixed - 57 zero; 8-bit
    path 516 = 605 - 59 zero - 29 quiet (+-1). Gate off
    (SDL_HINT_DOS_SILENCE_DETECT=0, UR6): no silent IRQs across two
    sound-9 plays, against 27 with it on.
  - With this patch and dosags driving the flag (DOSBox-X --sb-live, cells
    CA16, CA16B, CA8): pcm_irqs equals the expected content chunks plus
    drains EXACTLY on both paths (16-bit 127/127 and 1298/1298, 8-bit
    1361/1361, zero windows included), no silent IRQ during any sound-9
    play (4 plays; the build without it: 37 over 3), idle silence still
    skipped (skipped_silent 5608-7638 per run), overwrites 0.
Hardware confirmation of the fix pending.

Why not the simpler alternatives:
  - Judging silence before format conversion would not help: a chunk that
    rounds to all 0x80 is also silent when played, so nothing audible is
    lost -- only TIME, the same defect as (a).
  - "Keep silence while the ring holds audio" cannot work: SDL3's playback
    iterate fills an empty stream with silence and still calls PlayDevice
    (SDL_audio.c, br < buffer_size -> memset), so after the first sound
    the ring would never empty and the gate would never skip again.
  - SDL_HINT_DOS_SILENCE_DETECT=0 (zero code) removes the loss but lets
    idle silence fill the ring to capacity, so every new sound queues
    behind up to a ring's worth (~0.74 s at the default depth) of silence.
What decides it is whether content is playing, and only the port's own
mixer knows that.

WHAT: SDL_DOSAudioSetContentActive(bool) (SDL_dosaudio_pump.h). While
true, PlayDevice skips the silence scan and writes silent buffers like
any other; the gate, its SDL_Delay(10) throttle and idle-pause are
untouched otherwise. Default false: a port that never calls it -- every
SDL_mixer port, and anything scaffolded from this series before now --
gets the gate's behaviour unchanged; the only other change on that path
is two counter increments. Two monotonic counters beside the other
per-IRQ audio counters (SDL_dos_audio_synth.h), for the port to report:
dos_port_audio_skipped_silent_count (buffers the gate dropped) and
dos_port_audio_idle_pause_count (DSP idle-pause commands issued).

Source: dosags patches/SDL/0192 (From 00a6f143b44b), re-derived here
against the hub series (line offset only). Comment tags renumbered
0192 -> 0143; the flag and setter moved above the SDL/0088 ring-fill
comment block rather than between that block and the function it
documents (placement only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
